format 1

# Seeded by `pklith seed --init` from the fragments this repository's
# files switch on (`pklith detect`). It is yours now: pklith never rewrites it.
#
# No built-in check reads these types yet, so `pklith check` names them
# until each gets checks or an exempt reason: envrc, format-upstream, gitignore, lock, spec-records.

## checks
id|category|nix|glob|check|fix|env|msg
lychee|lint|lychee|**/*.md|lychee --offline --no-progress {{files}}|-|-|a markdown link points at a file or anchor that does not exist; fix the link (offline: external URLs are not fetched)
gen-check|gate|-|.pklith, hk.pklith.pkl, nix/pklith.nix|pklith gen --check|pklith gen|-|hk.pklith.pkl or nix/pklith.nix no longer matches .pklith; run pklith gen
spec-records|spec|microlith|SPEC.md, .spec-records|mth check --records .spec-records SPEC.md|-|-|a rejected option recorded in .spec-records was edited out of SPEC.md; restore the record or remove it from .spec-records in its own reviewed commit
ceiling-cap|spec|gawk|.context-limits, nix/ceiling-cap.awk|awk -f nix/ceiling-cap.awk .context-limits|-|-|a .context-limits ceiling is over its cap (SPEC.md file 3500, chain 5500); split the node with sherd split instead of raising (nix:V3)
ctrm|lint|-|**/*|ctrm check {{files}}|ctrm fix {{files}}|-|a file holds a character its set does not grant; fix it, or grant it in .ctrm and say why in the commit (nix:V12)
xnl-check|lint|-|**/*.nix, **/*.pkl, **/*.awk, .envrc, .githooks/*|xnl check {{files}}|-|-|a host file embeds a non-trivial program in another language; extract it with xnl extract (nix:V13)
xnl-lint|lint|-|**/*.nix, **/*.pkl, **/*.awk, .envrc, .githooks/*|xnl lint {{files}}|xnl lint --fix {{files}}|-|an embedded or extracted program fails its own language's linter (nix:V13)
rekall|lint|-|AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, rekall.toml|rekall check|-|-|agent prose drifted from the rules rekall extracted from it; run rekall scan and settle the drift (nix:V14)
cargo-test|test|-|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, dev/Cargo.toml|cargo test --workspace --quiet|-|-|a test fails; fix the code or, if the spec changed, backprop it first
rust-mirror|lint|-|**/*.rs, nix/guard/rust-mirror.sh|bash nix/guard/rust-mirror.sh|-|-|a Rust file with logic has no sibling tests.rs wired by #[cfg(test)] mod tests; (nix:V6)
module-size|lint|-|**/*.rs, nix/guard/module-size.sh|bash nix/guard/module-size.sh|-|-|a Rust module is over 500 code lines or 1000 lines; split it (nix:V16)
tdd-order|coverage|-|**/*.rs, nix/guard/tdd-order.sh, nix/guard/tdd-order.exempt|bash nix/guard/tdd-order.sh|-|-|a commit adds Rust code with no test: commit before it in the push range (nix:V7)
coverage|coverage|-|**/*.rs, .coverage, nix/guard/coverage.sh|bash nix/guard/coverage.sh|bash nix/guard/coverage.sh --fix|-|line coverage is below the floor, or .coverage overstates or lags the measurement (nix:V5)
cargo-deny|lint|-|Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, deny.toml, dev/Cargo.toml|cargo deny --all-features check bans licenses sources advisories|-|-|a dependency breaks deny.toml: banned or duplicate version, licence outside the allow list, unknown source, or advisory (nix:V10)
pklith-check|coverage|-|**/*|pklith check|-|-|a tracked file type has no row in .pklith, a row matches nothing, or a claimed check never reaches its files

## types
type|checks|min|exempt
*|trailing-whitespace, final-newline, line-endings, no-bom, no-merge-conflict, no-case-conflict, no-broken-symlinks, no-private-key, ripsecrets, typos, editorconfig-checker, no-local-paths, itok, pklith-check, ctrm|-|-
editorconfig|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
gitattributes|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
md|markdownlint, lychee|-|-
nix|nixfmt, statix, deadnix|-|-
path:**/SPEC.md|markdownlint, mth-fmt, mth-check, sherd-check, sherd-nav, sherd-budget|-|-
path:.context-limits|sherd-budget, ceiling-cap|-|-
pklith|gen-check|-|-
pkl|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
pre-commit|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
pre-push|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
path:.envrc|-|-|one line `use flake`; direnv evaluates it
path:.gitignore|-|-|ignore patterns, no syntax to check
path:flake.lock|-|-|generated by `nix flake lock`
path:.format-upstream|-|-|vendored record copied from microlith v0.7.4
path:.spec-records|spec-records|-|-
path:FORMAT.md|-|-|vendored from microlith v0.7.4, unmodified (`.format-upstream`)
path:FORMAT-EXTENSIONS.md|-|-|vendored from microlith v0.7.4, unmodified
path:SPEC-PROMPT.md|-|-|historical input, kept unchanged
path:.markdownlintignore|-|-|ignore list read by markdownlint, no syntax to check
path:.ctrm|-|-|ctrm config, read and validated by the ctrm step on every file
path:.ctrm-sets|-|-|ctrm set declarations, read and validated by the ctrm step
path:rekall.toml|rekall, taplo|-|-
path:AGENTS.md|markdownlint, rekall|-|-
toml|taplo|-|-
awk|gawk-lint|-|-
rs|rustfmt, clippy, cargo-test, rust-mirror, module-size, tdd-order, coverage|-|-
path:Cargo.lock|cargo-deny|-|-
path:Cargo.toml|taplo, cargo-deny|-|-
path:dev/Cargo.toml|taplo, cargo-deny|-|-
path:deny.toml|taplo, cargo-deny|-|-
sh|shellcheck, shfmt|-|-
path:.coverage|coverage|-|-
path:nix/guard/tdd-order.exempt|tdd-order|-|-
yaml|yamllint|-|-
